5. Theorem 3.1 (block class).  Per block, the exact Bayes value as a function of the expected
   number x of questions in the block is the lower convex envelope E1(x) of the single-block points;
   for m blocks and n questions the uniform-prior Bayes value is E1(n/m) (blocks are independent
   under the prior, and E1 is convex).  Theorem 3.1 claims p(1 - 2L/N - 2x/N) <= E1(x).
   inequality holds on all grid points; smallest ratio E1/bound where the bound is positive: 1.1111
